  "question": {
    "text": "The number of numbers, lying between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>99</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn></math>&nbsp;that can&nbsp;be made from the digits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> when the digits occur only once in each number, is",
